 "scenery": [],
 "par": {
  "time": 480
 },
 "intro": {
  "title": "MOURNING HALLS",
  "lines": [
   "A cloister with a garden of graves, and a chapel at every corner with somebody in it.",
   "There is not much left to shoot with. There is not much to shoot."
  ]
 },
 "outro": "The lift came to the bottom and stopped. The shaft is a long way down. The east door of the hall had unlocked itself by then.",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "start",
   "at": [35, 11],
   "radius": 5,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A cloister. The arcade is low and the garden in the middle is full of stones with names cut in them in a hand I can't read. There's a candle lit at every corner of the building."
  },
  {
   "id": "count",
   "at": [35, 14],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "TALLY PLATE",
   "text": "THE SILENT IN THIS HOUSE: 6. TO THE LIFT, ON THE CALL. A number is crossed out and written again in the margin: 4."
  },
  {
   "id": "plan",
   "at": [14, 12],
   "radius": 6,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The four chapels are at the corners. Each has a latch on the far wall, beside the candles. When all four are thrown the call goes out."
  },
  {
   "id": "hunt",
   "at": [1, 1],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "A bell has gone in the south arm, three strokes. The Songkeepers on the rounds have stopped walking and turned to face the north-west chapel."
  },
  {
   "id": "zealot",
   "at": [9, 13],
   "radius": 6,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Songkeepers in the arcade, in pairs, walking the rounds. They are looking for what the chapels hold, and not for me yet."
  },
  {
   "id": "c1",
   "at": [1, 1],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The latch is thrown. The cell behind the altar is empty. The bench is still warm."
  },
  {
   "id": "c2",
   "at": [1, 1],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The second latch. A cup on the floor, still wet. Whoever it held went out by the arcade without a sound."
  },
  {
   "id": "c3",
   "at": [1, 1],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The third latch. The cell is open and there is a folded cloth on the bench. The candle beside it has just been lit."
  },
  {
   "id": "c4",
   "at": [1, 1],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The fourth latch. Every cell in the house is open now."
  },
  {
   "id": "call",
   "at": [1, 1],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The horn at the south end has sounded the call. The Silent are going to the lift in the gate hall."
  },
  {
   "id": "door-shut",
   "at": [35, 60],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The door at the head of the stair to the gate hall is shut. It opens to the call, and the call is the fourth latch."
  },
  {
   "id": "hall",
   "at": [35, 71],
   "radius": 6,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The gate hall. The lift shaft is behind the last row of pews: the rail will keep you out of it. Stay behind the rail."
  },
  {
   "id": "door",
   "at": [51, 75],
   "radius": 5,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The way out is sealed until the lift has gone down. It does not need a key or a lever. It needs the Silent to be gone.",
   "unless": [
    "msg:gone"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s1",
   "at": [1, 1],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "A SILENT",
   "text": "I will not sing it. I sang it forty years and it was never mine."
  },
  {
   "id": "s2",
   "at": [1, 1],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "A SILENT",
   "choice": "halls=silent",
   "text": "You are the one who came by the low halls. You asked nothing of us. I will not count you."
  },
  {
   "id": "s2b",
   "at": [1, 1],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "A SILENT",
   "choice": "halls!=silent",
   "text": "You went through the gallery. I heard what was left of it. I will not thank you and I do not blame you."
  },
  {
   "id": "s3",
   "at": [1, 1],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "A SILENT",
   "text": "I will not answer. Whoever calls, I will stand here."
  },
  {
   "id": "s4",
   "at": [1, 1],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "A SILENT",
   "choice": "halls=silent",
   "text": "I will not forget the ones who sang. I have kept them in order. Carry a light, low. They follow it, and they do not ring it."
  },
  {
   "id": "s5",
   "at": [1, 1],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "A SILENT",
   "choice": "halls=silent",
   "text": "Thank you for the quiet."
  },
  {
   "id": "s6",
   "at": [1, 1],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "A SILENT",
   "choice": "halls=silent",
   "text": "Go down. Do not wait for us."
  },
  {
   "id": "gone",
   "at": [1, 1],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "They didn't look at me, and they didn't look back. Forty feet down the shaft the light of the lift went out, one lamp at a time."
  },
  {
   "id": "bells",
   "at": [21, 30],
   "radius": 5,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "In the garden a tree of glass, and three chimes among the graves. The tree plays three notes when you use it: answer on the chimes, in order, each within eight seconds of the last."
  },
  {
   "id": "niche-open",
   "at": [1, 1],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "A door has opened in the west wall of the arcade, and behind it a closet with a lamp left burning."
  },
  {
   "id": "niche",
   "at": [8, 35],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "A SILENT (NOTE)",
   "text": "The bells were for the ones who went down in the lift, and nobody has rung them. I left the tin for whoever did. It is not much."
  },
  {
   "id": "hollow",
   "at": [35, 9],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The north wall of the arcade rings hollow in one run of cells. There is a door in it, painted over."
  },
  {
   "id": "g1",
   "at": [35, 4],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "A SILENT (NOTE)",
   "text": "My sister is under the third stone. She sang the count at the Gate for twenty years and stopped on the day it asked her to sing me. They put her here. I took the next house along."
  },
  {
   "id": "g2",
   "at": [33, 4],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "A SILENT (NOTE)",
   "text": "I tend the stones. Nobody comes. The ones who sang are kept in order by size, and the Silent in order by the day they stopped. She is first. I am not on the list yet."
  },
  {
   "id": "g3",
   "at": [37, 4],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "A SILENT (NOTE)",
   "text": "If you are the one with the lamp, put it here for the length of one candle. Then take it with you. She was afraid of the dark at the end, and I never got it right."
  },
  {
   "id": "ossuary",
   "at": [9, 46],
   "radius": 2,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A bone-room behind the crack, the cloister's own ossuary. Someone left a vest and a mend on the shelf of skulls, which is either respect or the opposite."
  }
 ],
 "objective": "Throw the latch in each of the four chapels, one at each corner of the cloister. Ammunition is low: spend it",
